# Component Naming

Follow [`packages/app/src/lib/components/`](packages/app/src/lib/components/) — same rules apply to [`packages/ui`](packages/ui) and [`packages/website/src/lib/components/`](packages/website/src/lib/components/).

## Files and folders

- **kebab-case** only — never `Button.svelte`, `Header.svelte`, `DownloadSection.svelte`, or `MatchTitle.svelte`
- Folder = scope: `ui/button`, `match`, `player`, `leaderboard`, `replay`, …
- Domain pieces: `{domain}-{piece}.svelte` — `match-title.svelte`, `leaderboard-list.svelte`
- Context modules: `context.ts`, `context.svelte.ts`, or `{domain}.context.svelte.ts`
- Barrels: always `index.ts`

## Website marketing components

Website-only site chrome lives under `packages/website/src/lib/components/` with the **same kebab-case rules**, grouped by folder — no PascalCase leftovers, no loose files on the components root:

| Folder | Files |
|---|---|
| `layout/` | `header.svelte`, `header-auth.svelte`, `footer.svelte`, `discord-menu.svelte` |
| `home/` | `hero.svelte`, `download-section.svelte`, `fair-play-section.svelte`, `feature-section.svelte` |
| `player/` | `card-form.svelte` plus player profile pieces |
| `ui/` | `error-state.svelte`, `map-image.svelte` |

Shared player/replay UI stays in scoped folders (`player/`, `replay/`, `player-performance/`, `ui/`) — already kebab-case.

## Script bindings vs exports

- Import binding: **PascalCase** (`MatchTitle` from `./match-title.svelte`)
- Compound families: namespace barrels — `export { MatchTitle as Title }` → `import * as Match`
- Simple primitives: named export — `import { Button } from '@company-of-heroes/ui/button'`

```typescript
// ✅ compound domain
import * as Match from '$lib/components/match';
// <Match.Root><Match.Title /></Match.Root>

// ✅ shared primitive (app re-exports or direct package import)
import { Button } from '@company-of-heroes/ui/button';
import { LeaderboardList } from '@company-of-heroes/ui/leaderboard';

// ✅ website marketing — folder + kebab path, PascalCase binding
import Header from '$lib/components/layout/header.svelte';
import DownloadSection from '$lib/components/home/download-section.svelte';
```

## Do not

- PascalCase filenames in `components/` or `packages/ui/src/`
- Loose domain files at the website `components/` root — put chrome in `layout/` or `home/`
- Duplicate shared UI in website/app when `@company-of-heroes/ui` already has it

## New shared components

Add to **`packages/ui`** first (presentational, no `$lib` / `$core` / `$app`). Host-specific fetch, i18n, and navigation stay in thin adapters under `packages/app` or website route containers.
